        "original_id": "b420188a-15bd-5921-810c-f4c59e8c1fc6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Columbia University, University of Colorado system, Harvard Law School, United States District Court for the District of Montana\n- People: Robert Cunningham Humphreys, Kurt Alme, Charles C. Lovell\n- Places: Upper Manhattan, New York City, Colorado, Denver, Aurora\n- Topics: universities, campuses, education, judicial clerkships\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754 as a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Columbia University is officially named Columbia University in the City of New York and is often cited as one of the world's most prestigious universities.\n- Robert Cunningham Humphreys was a student at Columbia University from 1926 to 1927.\n- The University of Colorado system is a public university system in Colorado with four campuses.\n- The University of Colorado system includes the University of Colorado Boulder, the University of Colorado Colorado Springs, and the University of Colorado Denver located in downtown Denver and at the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora.\n- Kurt Alme graduated from the University of Colorado and Harvard Law School.\n- Kurt Alme clerked for Charles C. Lovell of the United States District Court for the District of Montana.",
